# StackPerch

> StackPerch, formerly KeepAny, is a local digital asset workspace for independent developers. It connects projects, domains recorded in project details, accounts, subscriptions, and maintenance.

## Product facts

- Local React application; English and Simplified Chinese interfaces.
- Local use does not require registration or payment.
- Source code uses AGPL-3.0-only; third-party materials retain their own licenses.
- Portable preview requires Node.js 22+ and runs at http://127.0.0.1:4180/.
- The repository and official website now use StackPerch addresses. The old KeepAny GitHub and public website entries remain compatible. New portable packages use the StackPerch name; older KeepAny packages remain available.
- The rename preserves browser storage at the same origin and profile. Existing KeepAny .ka1 backups and .kdbx vaults remain usable with their original passwords.
- Browser data is separated by origin and profile. Clearing site data can remove it. Download and verify encrypted .ka1 backups.
- A separate encrypted KDBX vault stores passwords and persistent model keys. It is excluded from ordinary assets, global search, MCP, and asset sync.
- AI is optional. The vault's explicitly approved full-text AI import sends the current list, which may include passwords and notes, to the selected provider. It does not send the existing vault or master password.
- Early preview: not independently security-audited, and not verified on every device or browser.
- Official cloud sync and paid services are not open. Optional hosting is planned; commercial expansion is paused.
- Password autofill, cross-device password sync, background email, and closed-page push are not provided.
- Experimental sync, account-binding, remote storage, and MCP are not necessary for local trial.

